DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("cos((e^((ln(x)))))");
$fun_1 = Formula("((sqrt(x)))^2");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("((-infinity, 17] - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-6, 1, 7, 8})) U {-6, 1, 7, 8}");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("{-6, 1, 7, 8} U {-6, 1, 7, 8} U (-infinity, 17]");
$set_ans_6 = Compute("(-infinity, 17] U {-6, 1, 7, 8} U {-6, 1, 7, 8}");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(7, infinity) U (7, infinity) U (7, infinity)");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("(-infinity, 10) U (-infinity, 10) U (((((-infinity, 10))) U (7, infinity)))");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("((7, infinity)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ((-infinity, 10))) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (((((7, infinity) U (-infinity, 10))))))");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`14+9-17+11`]? [_____]{answer=>Real(17.),width=>2}
---

What is the value of [`16+2-18-13/2`]? [_____]{answer=>Real(-6.5),width=>10}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x > 6\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x < 10\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup A \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B \cup B \cup ((((B)) \cup A)) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`(A) \cap (B) \cap ((((A \cup B)))) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x \leq 17\}`]
- [`B = \{-6, 1, 7, 8\}`]

Compute:
- [`(A \cap B) \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`B \cup B \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}
- [`A \cup B \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_6}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -2, 9, 10 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 7, 6, 9 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<7, 6, 9>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-2, 9, 10>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<7, 6, 9>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, 6, 9>") . Compute("<-2, 9, 10>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 1, 7, 4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 5, -5, -4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 1, 2, -1 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<5, -5, -4>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<1, 7, 4>") x Compute("<5, -5, -4>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<1, 7, 4>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<1, 2, -1>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<1, 2, -1>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{w} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<1, 2, -1>"))}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(7) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>7)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(3) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>3)}
- [`f'(5) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>5)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
